From: NWA50BE recovery-kit build guard
Subject: [PATCH] ipq53xx: use the central initramfs device list

TIP's ipq53xx target is linked from an external feed that also contains an
empty linux/generic directory.  GENERIC_PLATFORM_DIR therefore points into
that feed, where image/initramfs-base-files.txt does not exist.  The nested
kernel build fails, while the surrounding lock helper continues and packages
a stale kernel.

Override the generic initramfs node list with the file shipped by the pinned
OpenWrt tree.

--- a/feeds/qca-wifi-7/ipq53xx/Makefile
+++ b/feeds/qca-wifi-7/ipq53xx/Makefile
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ SUBTARGETS:=generic ipq53xx_32
 
 KERNELNAME:=Image dtbs
 KERNEL_PATCHVER:=6.6
+INITRAMFS_EXTRA_FILES:=$(TOPDIR)/target/linux/generic/image/initramfs-base-files.txt
 #KERNEL_NAME_SUFFIX=-0c8ca76b942082e176fe07ddf18a7a5413b1612a
 
 include $(INCLUDE_DIR)/target.mk
